  "body": "Just found the there's a bit different from the computed value of `color` property and that of `-webkit-text-fill-color`. The computed value of `-webkit-text-fill-color` might need to be updated to be the same as [color property specification](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-3/#foreground).\r\n\r\nAs to the `-webkit-text-stroke-width`, would it be better to update the `Animatable: no` to be `Animation type: discrete`?\r\n\r\nQuoted from  @SebastianZ \"The W3C decided [some time ago](https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/www-style/2015Nov/0308.html)  to replace the \"animatable\" info by an \"animation type\" [with \"discrete\" as value](https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/www-style/2016May/0121.html) when they have a discrete value transition.\"\r\n\r\nWe shall probably update all the 'animatable' info in this specification as well. (Maybe in another issue?)",
